### Timeline Extended: the mod's centred popups (Space Race UI pass design § 3,
### docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-31-space-race-ui-pass-design.md). Additive: a
### scripted widget (gui/scripted_widgets/te_systems_window.txt registers the
### root), so no vanilla file is replaced.
###
### te_popups  a full-size root on the popups layer, above the journal panel,
###            the side panels and the Timeline Extended window. It is up only
###            while a popup is open, for a played country (as the Timeline
###            Extended window's root), and holds one instance of each popup
###            type. Each derives from te_ui_popup (gui/te_widget_library.gui)
###            and shows on its own value of te_popup.
###
### STATE. te_popup is a client-side GetVariableSystem value (never saved): the
### open popup, one at a time. Set by the button that opens a popup, cleared by
### its close button, Escape and a click outside. Values:
###   sr_target          Solar System Colonization's colony target
###                      (te_sr_target_popup, space_race_widget.gui)
###   sr_dest_<n>        fleet slot n's destination (te_sr_dest_popup,
###                      space_race_widget.gui; its bodies are generated by
###                      gen_space_fleets.py, one a slot)
###   sr_ftarget_<n>     fleet slot n's target world (te_sr_ftarget_popup,
###                      likewise)
###   sr_xfer_<n>        a fleet's Transfer (n its slot, 1 to 9; te_sr_xfer_popup,
###                      space_race_widget.gui, its bodies generated by
###                      gen_space_fleets)
### --- Help pages (charts-help-national-info plan, PRs H1 and H2) --------
###   help_<key>         a system's Help page, te_<key>_help_popup (a
###                      te_ui_help_popup), in the system's widget file: its
###                      "How X Works" section, now a link, and the "?" in its
###                      tab's header open it. A page reads GetPlayer only, so
###                      it needs none of the gate and datacontext below.
###                      Pages: banking, grand_monuments, colonial_empire,
###                      cultural_hegemony, nuclear_weapons,
###                      strategic_reserve, seabed, covert_warfare, nation,
###                      budget_breakdown, united_nations, demographics
###                      (test_te_help_pages.py's PAGES).
### --- end Help pages ------------------------------------------------------
###
### A popup has no journal entry of its own, so each body sits under the entry's
### scope-free gate and a GetPlayerJournalEntry datacontext on a child, as the
### Timeline Extended window's tabs do (gui_modding_guide.md gotchas #22, #29):
### the rows' JournalEntry.GetCountry reads then work as in the panel.

widget = {
	name = "te_popups"
	size = { 100% 100% }
	layer = popups
	visible = "[And( And( GetMetaPlayer.GetPlayedOrObservedCountry.IsValid, Not( GetMetaPlayer.IsObserver ) ), GetVariableSystem.Exists('te_popup') )]"

	te_sr_target_popup = {}
	te_sr_dest_popup = {}
	te_sr_ftarget_popup = {}
	te_sr_xfer_popup = {}

	### --- Help pages (charts-help-national-info plan, PRs H1 and H2) ----
	te_banking_help_popup = {}
	te_grand_monuments_help_popup = {}
	te_colonial_empire_help_popup = {}
	te_cultural_hegemony_help_popup = {}
	te_nuclear_weapons_help_popup = {}
	te_strategic_reserve_help_popup = {}
	te_seabed_help_popup = {}
	te_covert_warfare_help_popup = {}
	te_nation_help_popup = {}
	te_budget_breakdown_help_popup = {}
	te_united_nations_help_popup = {}
	te_demographics_help_popup = {}
	### --- end Help pages ---------------------------------------------------
}
